    "narrative": "For June 7, the Austin Waves lineup is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (71.95) and **Jackson Merrill** (67.27), who represent our highest-ceiling plays against their respective right-handed matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an aggressive assessment of Kevin Gausman\u2019s delivery speed, which presents a high-probability environment for him to exploit the stolen base category\u2014our primary scarcity driver. Meanwhile, **Jackson Merrill** draws a favorable profile against the opposing right-hander; despite a slight negative adjustment for the catcher's pop time, the wind blowing out and his advantageous spot in the two-hole make him a high-efficiency start. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.47) and **Kyle Tucker** (66.74) round out our top-tier core, providing the reliable production needed to stabilize our weekly Roto standings.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Nolan Schanuel** (44.18), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Miguel Andujar** and **Miguel Vargas**. While **Nolan Schanuel** remains a viable depth piece, the optimizer favored **Miguel Andujar**\u2019s situational boost from favorable wind conditions, and **Miguel Vargas**\u2019s spot in the batting order, despite facing a tougher opponent in Aaron Nola. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (64.40) and **Josh Jung** (60.61) also warrant attention; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** earns a significant boost from a strong platoon advantage against Soroka, while **Josh Jung**\u2019s high score is driven largely by his placement in the two-hole and an favorable expected ERA from the opposing starter, Cantillo.\n\nWe are monitoring the risk profile of **Liam Hicks** (46.39) closely, as he sits near the lower threshold of our daily start floor. His score is bolstered by an leadoff opportunity, but he remains a high-variance play given the quality of the opposing starter. As we navigate the remainder of the week, we continue to prioritize volume and speed, keeping bench options like **Dominic Smith** and **Brayan Rocchio** sidelined as they failed to clear our 40.0 efficiency threshold against today's difficult pitching slate. Managers should ensure all lineup confirmations are locked in, specifically keeping an eye on **Sam Antonacci** as he looks to exploit the matchups against Nola.",
